<title>USA: PECO asks regultor to back securitiation plan.</title>
<headline>PECO asks regultor to back securitiation plan.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>PECO Energy Co said Thursday it has asked the Pennsylvania Public Utility Commission to approve its request to securitize long-term debt and, it said, to lower customer electric bills.</p>
<p>The company made the request in legal papers filed that describe an administrative law judge's recommendation as &quot;severely flawed.&quot;  The judge recommended, on April 14, that the company's application to refinance $3.6 billion of its $6.75 billion total in stranded costs be denied in its entirety.</p>
<p>PECO said that securitization would bring relief to customers, lowering electric rates by $111 million, or 3.4 percent annually.</p>
</text>
